# The parquet stores under store/ ARE versioned, by choice -- git is the
# off-machine copy of data that cannot be re-fetched.
#
# Measured churn per harvest: 1,500 files / ~204 MB genuinely change (750 daily
# + 750 current-month intraday), because one new bar recompresses a whole
# parquet file. Closed months are rewritten byte-identically and cost nothing.
# Committing every run would be ~51 GB/year, so run_daily.ps1 delegates to
# snapshot_store.ps1, which commits monthly (~2.5 GB/year).
#
# store/intraday/ is the irreplaceable part: once a session falls outside NSE's
# ~20-session window it cannot be re-fetched at any price. store/daily/ can be
# rebuilt any time with `python backfill_eod.py`.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
